Module load components
Entry pointer on cell zero and exit pointer on cell zero
Reads the components bytes up to the first zero byte and makes one element per byte
Element layout is fifteen cells starting at cell seventy five and each element is fifteen cells apart
Lanes zero data; one to three work cells kept zero; four query carry; five to seven work and carry cells;
eight cursor; nine staging; ten not cursor; eleven name first flag; twelve in table marker;
thirteen layout store; fourteen status carry
Cell sixty four is the IO cell and cell seventy two is the HOME marker which stays zero
Cell eighty one holds one before the loop so the first header name is recognised

